+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Orders currently support creation, lookup, payment and cancellation, and coupons can be administered, but there is no way to redeem a coupon against an order. Customers expect to apply a coupon code at checkout and have the discount reflected in the order's final amount.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- Validate the coupon before applying it: it must exist, be `ACTIVE`, be within its validity window, and the order's amount must meet the coupon's `min_amount_cents`.
+- Compute the discount: `FIXED` subtracts a fixed amount of cents; `PERCENT` takes a percentage of the order amount (honouring `max_discount_cents` when set).
+- Persist the applied coupon code, discount and resulting final amount on the order, and record the redemption against the coupon.
+- Return the updated order on success (HTTP 200); reject any invalid coupon with HTTP 400.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupon`: Applying a coupon code to an order, including eligibility rules (existence, active status, validity window, minimum amount) and discount computation for FIXED and PERCENT coupons.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None: no existing specs exist in this project. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts`: new route registration.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts`: coupon application business rules (needs access to coupons and the clock).
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts`: persist discount, final amount and coupon code; `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`: record redemption and increment usage.
+- `src/app.ts`: wire the coupon repository/clock into `OrderService`.
+- HTTP API surface: new endpoint on the existing order resource.
